schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Security Best Practices for Organizations Using Crypto Wallets
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  summary: >-
    Security guidance for regenerative organizations holding crypto assets:
    the core rule is no single point of failure, achieved via multi-sig
    wallets (e.g. Safe) with configurations from 2-of-3 to 4-of-7 depending on
    org size; layered role-based access control (operations/managers/
    executives/board); separation of hot wallets (2-4 weeks of operating
    funds) from cold-storage treasury reserves; a written policy framework
    (digital-asset management, security protocols, emergency response,
    smart-contract vetting); and ongoing team training on phishing and safe
    transaction practices. Includes a practical security checklist and an
    explicit warning against using personal wallets for organizational funds.
  audience: DAO operators / regenerative organizations managing crypto treasuries
  known_tensions: []
  related_concepts:
    - no-single-point-of-failure
  related_resources:
    - safe
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/security-best-practices-orgs.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
